cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mvula, please cite this software release."
title: "Mvula: compressing ECMWF AIFS for laptop-scale African weather experimentation"
version: 5.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-22"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/msovara/lapai-forecast-africa"
url: "https://codeforearth.ecmwf.int/project/mvula/"
abstract: >-
  Public citable snapshot of Mvula v5 (ECMWF Code for Earth 2026, African
  Stream). The Track B student is about 8.8 MiB and is evaluated as one-step,
  analysis-forced African 2 m temperature on a laptop CPU. This release does
  not claim a free-run, autoregressive, or 10-day forecast, full 65-channel
  output, precipitation skill, or smartphone deployment. Third-party AIFS
  teacher weights are not included and remain under their original terms.
  Source code is Apache-2.0; documentation in the repository is CC BY 4.0.
authors:
